WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:16.200
If you have hyperlipidemia, commonly known as "high cholesterol,"

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:19.440
you have high levels of lipids in your blood.

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:22.660
Lipids are fats and fat-like substances.

00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:29.560
In this condition, the most common types of lipids are cholesterol and triglycerides.

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:35.580
Your body needs cholesterol to function properly.

00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:40.220
It makes all the cholesterol you need, mostly in your liver.

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:47.220
The cells in your body need cholesterol as part of their cell membrane.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:53.900
Your skin uses sunlight and cholesterol to make vitamin D.

00:00:54.940 --> 00:00:59.300
Certain glands, such as the testicles in men, and the adrenal glands,

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:03.600
use cholesterol to make important chemicals, called hormones.

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:12.320
And, your liver uses cholesterol to make bile acids, which help to digest fat in the food you eat.

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:17.880
Your body uses triglycerides for energy.

00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:22.020
Triglycerides in your blood come from food and your liver.

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:25.140
Foods high in triglycerides include:

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:31.680
fatty foods, refined carbohydrates, foods high in simple sugars, and alcohol.

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:39.320
From your liver, your lipids are not able
to move through your bloodstream without some adjustment.

00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:41.080
To enable their movement,

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:44.720
your liver wraps certain proteins around the lipids.

00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:49.360
The resulting new molecule, called a lipoprotein,

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:54.300
can move through your bloodstream and throughout your body to the cells that need it.

00:01:55.569 --> 00:01:59.289
Depending on which type of lipoprotein your cholesterol is part of,

00:01:59.289 --> 00:02:03.089
determines whether your cholesterol is "good" or "bad."

00:02:03.089 --> 00:02:07.520
For example, your liver makes very low-density lipoproteins,

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:08.980
or VLDLs,

00:02:08.980 --> 00:02:12.940
which are the source of "bad" cholesterol, or LDL.

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:18.340
These lipoproteins are stuffed with cholesterol and triglycerides.

00:02:22.220 --> 00:02:27.460
VLDL travels through your bloodstream, delivering triglycerides to your cells,

00:02:27.460 --> 00:02:29.920
which use them for energy.

00:02:33.220 --> 00:02:37.820
If your liver makes more VLDL than your body needs for energy,

00:02:37.820 --> 00:02:42.400
the VLDL stores the extra triglycerides as body fat.

00:02:45.220 --> 00:02:52.220
After losing its triglycerides, a VLDL becomes a low-density lipoprotein, or LDL.

00:02:52.580 --> 00:02:58.239
LDL travels through your bloodstream, delivering
cholesterol to the cells that need it.

00:02:58.469 --> 00:03:02.849
If your body makes too much LDL, it can build
up in your blood.

00:03:03.239 --> 00:03:08.919
LDL can deposit in the walls of your blood
vessels, causing a buildup of fatty material,

00:03:08.920 --> 00:03:10.160
called plaque.

00:03:10.780 --> 00:03:15.380
Damage to vessel walls can make it easier for LDL to form plaques.

00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:20.680
Over time, this build up can narrow the blood vessel

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:22.460
and reduce blood flow.

00:03:22.460 --> 00:03:26.120
This is why LDL is called the "bad" cholesterol.

00:03:26.599 --> 00:03:30.739
A common place this plaque can build up is in your coronary arteries,

00:03:30.739 --> 00:03:33.999
which are the blood vessels that feed your heart muscle.

00:03:34.340 --> 00:03:37.340
This build-up causes coronary artery disease

00:03:37.349 --> 00:03:39.969
and increases your risk of a heart attack.

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:43.080
Plaque in other arteries,

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:44.900
such as the carotid arteries in your neck,

00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:47.460
can reduce blood flow to your brain

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:49.540
and increase the risk of a stroke.

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:53.580
Your liver also makes high-density lipoprotein,

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:55.180
or HDL,

00:03:55.180 --> 00:03:57.900
also known as the "good" cholesterol.

00:03:58.180 --> 00:04:02.860
HDL has more protein and very little cholesterol and triglycerides

00:04:02.860 --> 00:04:04.700
compared to LDL.

00:04:08.860 --> 00:04:12.460
HDL helps remove excess cholesterol from your cells

00:04:15.320 --> 00:04:17.760
and from plaque in your blood vessels.

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:21.600
This is why HDL is called the "good" cholesterol.

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:25.780
HDL returns the excess cholesterol to your liver,

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:28.680
which removes it from your body.

00:04:31.140 --> 00:04:33.100
If you are 20 years of age or older,

00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:37.880
the National Institutes of Health recommends you have a blood test every five years,

00:04:37.890 --> 00:04:40.610
called a fasting lipoprotein profile.

00:04:40.610 --> 00:04:43.430
It measures your levels of total cholesterol,

00:04:44.980 --> 00:04:46.180
LDL,

00:04:47.480 --> 00:04:48.580
HDL,

00:04:49.980 --> 00:04:51.640
and triglycerides.

00:04:55.080 --> 00:04:58.120
During this test, a blood sample will be taken

00:04:58.120 --> 00:05:02.740
from your arm or finger after you have not
eaten for nine to twelve hours.

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:10.600
The total cholesterol goal should be less
than 200 milligrams per deciliter.

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:16.910
For most people, an ideal HDL, or "good" cholesterol,
should be 60 or higher.

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:22.880
An ideal LDL, or "bad" cholesterol, should
be less than 100.

00:05:23.240 --> 00:05:27.420
And fasting triglycerides should be less than
150.

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:31.800
Your specific goals may vary depending on your health situation.

00:05:31.800 --> 00:05:35.620
Ask your doctor what your lipid goals should be.

00:05:38.340 --> 00:05:41.060
If your cholesterol levels are too high,

00:05:41.060 --> 00:05:45.120
it's important to eat a heart-healthy diet
with lean sources of protein

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:47.640
and plenty of fruits and vegetables.

00:05:49.500 --> 00:05:53.340
Also, the types of fats you eat can affect your cholesterol level.

00:05:55.740 --> 00:05:59.000
For example, saturated fats and trans-fats

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:02.220
tend to raise LDL cholesterol in your blood.

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:07.160
These fats are usually solid at room temperature

00:06:07.160 --> 00:06:12.680
and are found in meat and dairy products,
many processed foods, and tropical oils

00:06:12.680 --> 00:06:16.160
such as coconut oil, palm oil, and cocoa butter.

00:06:18.760 --> 00:06:24.020
Unsaturated fats, including polyunsaturated and monounsaturated fats,

00:06:24.020 --> 00:06:28.300
are healthier fats that are usually more liquid at room temperature.

00:06:28.300 --> 00:06:31.320
They are found in foods such as fish, nuts,

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:32.960
and vegetable oils.

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:38.940
Other lifestyle decisions you can make to help your cholesterol are

00:06:38.940 --> 00:06:40.260
not smoking,

00:06:43.240 --> 00:06:47.260
and getting regular exercise, such as brisk walking or running.

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:56.680
If lifestyle changes can't reduce your cholesterol level enough,

00:06:56.680 --> 00:07:00.580
your doctor may prescribe certain medications to reduce it.

00:07:01.170 --> 00:07:05.970
Statins are drugs that reduce the amount of
cholesterol made in your liver.

00:07:05.970 --> 00:07:10.690
They affect LDL levels more than HDL or triglyceride
levels.

00:07:12.340 --> 00:07:19.720
Niacin reduces LDL cholesterol and triglycerides, and increases HDL cholesterol made in your liver.

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:25.280
Bile acid binding resins are drugs that prevent

00:07:25.280 --> 00:07:28.860
the re-use of bile after helping to digest
your food.

00:07:29.040 --> 00:07:33.440
As a result, your liver uses more cholesterol to replace the lost bile,

00:07:33.440 --> 00:07:36.800
which means less cholesterol in your bloodstream.

00:07:38.940 --> 00:07:43.800
Fibrates are mainly used to reduce triglyceride levels in your blood,

00:07:43.800 --> 00:07:46.440
but they can also raise HDL levels.

00:07:48.600 --> 00:07:55.640
Cholesterol absorption inhibitors reduce the amount of cholesterol absorbed by your intestines from the food you eat.

00:07:59.980 --> 00:08:05.960
In many cases, the same steps can help maintain healthy cholesterol and triglyceride levels,

00:08:05.960 --> 00:08:07.120
such as:

00:08:07.300 --> 00:08:11.420
eating a diet low in saturated fat, trans-fat, and cholesterol,

00:08:13.660 --> 00:08:15.500
getting regular exercise,

00:08:17.700 --> 00:08:19.340
managing your weight,

00:08:21.140 --> 00:08:22.840
and not smoking.

